<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cantabrian Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">29–19 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cantabrian Wars were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s final conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>, fought from 29 to 19 BCE against the Cantabri and Astures of the northern mountains. Augustus took personal command in 26–25 BCE, and his general Agrippa completed the subjugation in 19 BCE after fierce resistance and repeated revolts. The north-west was then organised within the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Tarraconensis, opening its gold mines to Roman exploitation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars.jpg" alt="Cantabrian Wars" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LLs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cantabrian_Wars.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
